% The work semi-naive evaluation does on a chain, as counted by -X stats.
% Round 0 runs only the rule that reads no path, and each round after it
% joins only the paths the round before derived, so every path is derived
% once, rather than once per pass as the naive fixed point in stats-naive.dl
% derives it.  The textual planner is chosen, and the Magic rewrite turned
% off, so that the counts measure the fixed point alone; stats-indexed.dl is
% the same program as the default planner runs it.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).
edge(c, d).
edge(d, e).
edge(e, f).
edge(f, g).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
